    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2QDdTfoDxMxaJgd9Y2t9Ap6)_\n\nFollow-up to #472.\n\n## Merge order\n- Independent of other open PRs; touches only `sp-fetch-inbox.el`, its literate doc and its tests.\n\n## Cause of the slowdown\n- The DEVONthink listing script (#472) called `r.name()`, `r.path()`, `r.kind()`, `r.type()`, `r.additionDate()`, `r.creationDate()`, `r.uuid()` on every record: about 8 Apple Events per record, versus 4 before.\n- Apple Events cost milliseconds each, so a big inbox with sub-groups adds up to seconds.\n- Cause inferred from reading the code; not measured, because DEVONthink and Emacs cannot run in the cloud container.\n\n## Changes\n- Listing script reads each field once per group for all children (`c.name()`, `c.additionDate()`, ...); still a single `osascript` call.\n- `sp-fetch-inbox--merge` uses a hash table instead of `member` over a list.\n- `sp-fetch-inbox-devonthink-depth` (default 8; 0 skips the sub-group walk).\n- `sp-fetch-inbox-profile`: when non-nil, messages the time of each step (DEVONthink script, parse, folder scan, merge, arrange) in `*Messages*`.\n- Sorting, `C-c s`, grouping and `C-c d` are unchanged; the items are still built once per command.\n\n## Second fix: `C-u M-x sp-fetch-inbox`\n- `sp-fetch-inbox--read-folder` already returns the folder name, but `sp-fetch-inbox` applied `cdr` to it: `and: Wrong type argument: listp, \"Texte Filosofia istoriei\"`.\n- Removed the `cdr`.\n\n## Tests (not run: no Emacs in the container)\n- Script reads in bulk (no `children()`, no `r.xxx()`), depth option.\n- 300 records + 300 files: one JXA call, no process calls.\n- Folder with spaces through `C-u` path; profile messages; merge dedup.\n\n## Manual testing\n- [ ] `M-x sp-fetch-inbox` opens noticeably faster than before\n- [ ] Set `(setq sp-fetch-inbox-profile t)`, run it, read `sp-fetch-inbox profile: DEVONthink script ...` in `*Messages*`\n- [ ] If the script is still slow, try `(setq sp-fetch-inbox-devonthink-depth 0)` and compare\n- [ ] Sub-group records still appear, grouped by sub-group\n- [ ] Sort by newest first still right; `C-c s` toggles A-Z\n- [ ] `C-c d` restricts to a folder\n- [ ] `C-u M-x sp-fetch-inbox`, choose a folder with spaces: no error, picker shows that folder only\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCXyk3bC6YPxjXfvkE)_",
